        "verifiedAt": "2026-09-23",
        "notes": "The PDF combines three separately paginated sheets: the Day observational competition (O1–O4, 4 problems, 1 hour, 100 points printed), the Night observational competition (O5–O6, 10 minutes, 50 points printed) and the Team Competition “Mountain” (no points printed). Therefore paper.totalPoints and paper.timeLimitMin are null; the printed totals and times are kept in paper.documentNotes (the two “Instructions” pages, p. 1 and p. 8). The year 2018 is not printed in the masthead; it is consistent with “March 21, 2018” in O3 and with the 12th IOAA. round is null because the catalogue value “observational” is not in the round vocabulary; roundType is observation although the Mountain task is a team practical (problemType practical). Parts: only O1 has printed sub-numbers (1)–(4), 20+5+10+5 = 40 points as printed. O4's Figures 4.1–4.4 each have an answer box but no printed sub-task labels, and O6 has five answer boxes without labels, so neither has parts; the catalogue's ~13 sub-tasks likely counted those boxes. The empty answer boxes and the “Answer：”/“Answers：” labels (printed with a full-width colon, and “Answer:” with an ASCII colon under Figure 4.4) are answer-sheet form elements and were not transcribed; the Mountain sheet's form lines “The height: ______ m; margin of error: ____ m.” and “Brief description of your process:” are kept in statementAfterParts, while “No. of Team:” and “Time of completion (for jury):” were omitted as jury form fields. Printed source quirks preserved: O1's first paragraph ends “in proportion to zenith distance” with no final period; the Mountain sheet prints “main concern ！” with a space and a full-width exclamation mark. The magnitude superscripts in O1 (5ᵐ, 1ᵐ - 3ᵐ, 2ᵐ) are written as LaTeX superscripts; the superscript “th” in “November 8th” is written inline as plain text. O5's first sentence is printed in bold, as is the whole O5 heading. The Mountain photo has no caption. No solutions file exists in the archive for this paper, so every solution is marked incomplete and no answers are given. No illegible passages."
      }
